// Kanto, entire — a ShowReel demonstration.
//
// Open on Pokémon Blue's title screen → pull back until all 226 maps of
// Kanto are in one frame → real swarm-run footage bursts out from the map
// coordinates where each moment happened → pull one clip forward and name
// it → end card.
//
// This file is a checked-in artifact of examples/kanto_reel.rs, which stays
// canonical: the map rectangles and the aspect-ratio arithmetic live there,
// not here. What lives here is the film itself, and comments on *why* a
// scene holds as long as it does or why a clip sits where it does — the
// storytelling reasoning a reader actually meets when they open this file.
// See examples/README.md for where each asset comes from and the evidence
// behind each clip's timestamp. `kanto_reel --check` guards this file
// against drifting from the Rust that produced it; it compares the two
// *parsed* films, so hand-written comments like these survive regeneration
// checks without being mistaken for drift (see src/timeline.rs for why).
